-- Provision-ProfilerSchema.sql
--
-- Creates and seeds the [Profiler] schema that profiler/ProfilerMain.bite and its sub-workflow
-- tree depend on. Companion to Resources/rabbit/Provision-ShovelBridgeSchema.sql, which does the
-- same job for RabbitProcess's dbo.jobs1.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS (WOLF-8512): the ShovelBridge load test was switched from RabbitProcess to
-- profiler/ProfilerMain, whose DB source points at WarewolfDevOpsTestDb - a database that had no
-- [Profiler] schema at all, so every SQL activity in the tree failed and Phase 4c had nothing to
-- verify. Provisioning was first done ad hoc against the live database, leaving no
-- source-controlled record; this script closes that gap so the database is reproducible.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT. Safe to re-run: tables and indexes are existence-guarded, procedures use
-- CREATE OR ALTER, and every seed block is the vendor's own MERGE (insert-or-update), so a
-- second run changes nothing.
--
-- Source of truth: C:/Builds/Unlimited.ProfilerServices/Database/Warewolf.ProfilerDB
--   Tables         -> Profiler/Tables/*.sql
--   Procedures     -> 'Profiler/Stored Procedures'/*.sql
--   Reference data -> Scripts/PostDeployments/Masters/Profiler/Seed*.sql
-- Table and seed ORDER below is load-bearing (FK dependencies) and mirrors that project's own
-- Script.PostDeployment.sql. Regenerate rather than hand-edit if the upstream project changes.
--
-- SCOPE: the 10 tables, 15 procedures and 1 function reachable from RequestForProfiling's call
-- path (which includes ProfilerMain), plus the reference data they read. The upstream project's
-- other views and functions (44 and 46 of them, mostly the holiday-calendar feature) are
-- deliberately omitted. Other procedures the staged .bite files name (usp_GetSpecialHolidays,
-- usp_AddSpecialHoliday, usp_SetScoresForWeekdayFailure, ...) are NOT reachable from
-- RequestForProfiling and are omitted too; Scripts/Tests/Provision-ProfilerSchema.Tests.ps1 fails the
-- moment a reachable one is missing.
--
-- usp_GetPublicHolidaysInDateRange and func_PublicHolidaysByYear were added after build 30853:
-- this header used to call the whole holiday-calendar feature unreferenced, but
-- GetTrackingPeriod.bite calls that procedure, and 54 of 200 burst messages failed on it.
--
-- usp_GetMandateProfilesDatesForDRIs, usp_GetMandateProfilesDatesForDRIsInitials and
-- usp_CheckIfHasRecommendationType were added later (WOLF-8512, build 30636/30638): the initial
-- cut of this script only covered the 11 procedures known at the time, missing three that the
-- .bite dependency closure had already staged as workflow resources but whose SQL bodies were
-- never carried across from the upstream project.
--
-- Reference data last regenerated 2026-10-07 from upstream develop at FS-992 (5fccd41): the
-- SeedProfileDates, SeedSpecialHolidays and SeedGrantDates blocks are verbatim copies of those
-- files. The SeedProfileDates block deletes rows absent from its source, so a stale copy here
-- removes upstream's newer collection dates from WarewolfDevOpsTestDb on the next pipeline
-- run - re-copy all three whenever upstream's seed files change.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

IF SCHEMA_ID('Profiler') IS NULL
    EXEC('CREATE SCHEMA [Profiler]');
GO


-- ========================= TABLES (dependency order) =========================


